---
description: Zoom maps by scaling the current picture, never by clearing it
alwaysApply: false
---
# Map zoom

Zoom must keep the picture that is already on screen and scale it. Do not reset the view on each wheel notch or pinch step.

Clearing tiles (`setZoomAround` with `animate: false`, or anything that hits `_resetView`) drops the current image and flashes the map background. That flash is the bug, even when the new tiles arrive quickly.

Do this instead:

- Scale the tiles already drawn (Leaflet zoom animation). While a zoom is in progress, update that animation (`_animateToZoom` / `_animateZoom`) instead of starting a second reset.
- Let a wheel notch or trackpad event change zoom immediately. Do not lock the gesture and make the next notch wait.
- Keep `zoomSnap` at `0` so the level can sit between integers. The +/- buttons can still move one whole level.
- Paint the map container a color close to the basemap, not a contrasting blue, so a one-frame gap is not a blue screen.

`SmoothZoom` in `src/CityMap/CityMapView.tsx` is the reference. Match it for any other Leaflet map in this project.
